    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d499">

                <pb facs="0475" n="377" xml:id="pg377"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Peirce to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-10-22"><hi rendition="#italic">October 22,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 347.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a
                    cutting from the Journal de St. Petersburg of this date, stating officially that
                    Mr. de Giers, the Russian minister to China, has returned to Pekin for the
                    purpose of entering as promptly as possible, in concert with the representatives
                    of the other powers, into negotiations with Li Hung Chang and Prince Tsin, the
                    plenipotentiaries of the Chinese Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herbert H. D.
                    Peirce.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d499-a1.xml" xpointer="d499-a1"/>
